{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "The current best is config_008 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc 0.725, 3.60 GPU-hrs). All four 'best' hyperparameters are already combined there, so marginal gains from further scvi_n200 variants (e.g., concat fusion, resnet50) are unlikely to exceed it. The major untested dimension in the top-performing architecture is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 has never been paired with the best image encoder + aggregation + fusion. Config_034 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_008. If PCA approaches 0.725, it would offer a cheaper alternative (PCA is a pre-computed linear transform, so no encoder training cost); if it falls well short, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and the remaining 2 experiments should focus on fine-tuning around the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer core. Expected relative cost: comparable to config_008 (~3–4 GPU-hrs), since the dominant cost is the ViT-L image encoder and transformer aggregation, and the 2000-dim PCA input adds only modest transformer overhead versus the 200-dim scvi latent."
}

